21,422,64,423],159.5262,1.446435,0.216196,[425,426,64,427],161.5203,1.447257,0.242544,[429,430,64,431],163.5143,1.447481,0.268792,[433,434,64,435],165.5084,1.447201,0.294946,[437,438,64,439],167.5025,1.446415,0.320998,[441,442,64,443],169.4966,1.445054,0.346922,[445,446,64,447],171.4906,1.443211,0.37273,[449,450,64,451],173.4847,1.440858,0.398406,[453,454,64,455],175.4788,1.437966,0.423934,[457,458,64,459],177.4729,1.434608,0.449323,[461,462,64,463],179.467,1.430735,0.474552,[465,466,64,467],181.461,1.426361,0.499615,[469,470,64,471],183.4551,1.421534,0.524519,[473,474,64,475],185.4492,1.41619,0.549232,[92,477,64,478],1.408636,0.58076,[480,481,64,482],189.4373,1.406036,0.587029,[484,481,64,482],191.4314,[486,481,64,482],193.4255,[488,481,64,482],195.4196,[490,481,64,482],197.4137,"Mars 3","ORBITER · LANDER · FLOWN","First spacecraft to soft-land on Mars","The Soviet Union's audacious double-mission to Mars in 1971 — Mars 2 and Mars 3 launched 9 days apart. Mars 2's lander crashed; Mars 3's lander achieved the first soft-landing on Mars but went silent ~110 seconds after touchdown — the actual transmission lasted only ~14.5 seconds — possibly due to the global dust storm raging at the time. The orbiter operated for 8 months, returning dozens of images and atmospheric measurements. Despite the brief surface mission, Mars 3 demonstrated that the descent and landing problem on Mars was solvable.",[496,500,503,507,510],{"met":64,"label":497,"note":498,"type":499},"LAUNCH","Proton-K with Blok-D upper stage from Baikonur.","nominal",{"met":12,"label":501,"note":502,"type":499},"ORBITER MOI","Orbiter captures into Mars orbit during global dust storm.",{"met":504,"label":505,"note":506,"type":499},188.005,"LANDER SEPARATION","Lander separates and begins atmospheric entry.",{"met":87,"label":508,"note":509,"type":499},"SURFACE CONTACT","First soft-landing on Mars; transmission begins.",{"met":92,"label":511,"note":512,"type":513},"SIGNAL LOSS","Signal lost ~110 s after touchdown (transmission lasted ~14.5 s). Cause unconfirmed; dust storm leading suspect.","warning","/orrery/images/missions/mars3/05.webp"],"uses":{"params":["id"]}}]}
